			(do_not_autoplace no)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
			)
		)
		(property "Description" "Addressable RGB LED (NeoPixel-compatible), Red key. Replaces the discrete LED+2SC1815+resistor driver. 2026-10-01: initially chose WS2812B 5050 SMD over SK6812MINI-E (the latter used in complicated_wires but hard to hand-solder); later changed to the full-size SK6812 5050 (same PLCC4 5.0x5.0mm package/footprint as WS2812B, same physical pin layout, but KiCad's stock SK6812 symbol numbers the pins differently -- pin1=VSS,2=DIN,3=VDD,4=DOUT vs WS2812B's 1=VDD,2=DOUT,3=VSS,4=DIN; verified against both stock library symbols before patching). Daisy-chained GP6->R10->D1->D2->D3->D4 (chain order = dict order Red/Blue/Green/Yellow); firmware addresses each LED by chain position, colour is software-assigned (not fixed by the LED itself). Pin1=VSS(GND), pin2=DIN, pin3=VDD(+5V), pin4=DOUT. Placed near the Red(left) key (not aligned to the switch's LED window -- user decision: thin keycap + indirect lighting, see four_button_design_notes.md)."
			(at 342.9 177.8 0)
			(hide yes)
			(show_name no)
			(do_not_autoplace no)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
			)
		)
		(pin "1"
			(uuid "530881e5-91ab-4207-b627-c67a39e3a0d2")
		)
		(pin "2"
			(uuid "71763144-af75-4ae4-aea9-d6a1b6ab31d7")
		)
